From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:53:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: Register only Glymur's full CSID/IFE
 pairs

Glymur uses the X1E80100 resource table, which registers three CSIDs,
two CSID Lites, two IFEs and two IFE Lites. On the ASUS Zenbook A16 only
the two full pairs stream with this driver:

- CSID2 has no IFE behind it, so no route through it delivers frames.
- The lite CSIDs are clocked by vfe_lite_csid and vfe_lite_cphy_rx, but
  the table gives them the full CSID clocks, so their receivers never
  see data.
- The driver pairs CSID n with IFE n for power-up, register update and
  buffer done. That is wrong for the lite blocks: CSID Lite0 is index 3
  and IFE Lite0 is index 2.

Give Glymur its own table with CSID0/1 and IFE0/1 until the lite blocks
are fixed, so userspace only sees entities that can stream. Both A16
cameras stream through CSID0/IFE0 and CSID1/IFE1 with this table.

Signed-off-by: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
index 8163dda..46e44e0 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -5815,6 +5815,27 @@ static const struct camss_resources x1e80100_resources = {
 	.vfe_num = ARRAY_SIZE(vfe_res_x1e80100),
 };
 
+/*
+ * Glymur shares X1E80100's blocks, but only the full CSID/IFE pairs stream with
+ * this driver: CSID2 has no IFE, and the lite pairs need their own clocks and
+ * CSID-to-IFE mapping.
+ */
+static const struct camss_resources glymur_resources = {
+	.version = CAMSS_X1E80100,
+	.pd_name = "top",
+	.csiphy_res = csiphy_res_x1e80100,
+	.tpg_res = tpg_res_x1e80100,
+	.csid_res = csid_res_x1e80100,
+	.vfe_res = vfe_res_x1e80100,
+	.csid_wrapper_res = &csid_wrapper_res_x1e80100,
+	.icc_res = icc_res_x1e80100,
+	.icc_path_num = ARRAY_SIZE(icc_res_x1e80100),
+	.csiphy_num = ARRAY_SIZE(csiphy_res_x1e80100),
+	.tpg_num = ARRAY_SIZE(tpg_res_x1e80100),
+	.csid_num = 2,
+	.vfe_num = 2,
+};
+
 static const struct of_device_id camss_dt_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8916-camss", .data = &msm8916_resources },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8939-camss", .data = &msm8939_resources },
@@ -5834,7 +5855,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id camss_dt_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8550-camss", .data = &sm8550_resources },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8650-camss", .data = &sm8650_resources },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,x1e80100-camss", .data = &x1e80100_resources },
-	{ .compatible = "qcom,glymur-camss", .data = &x1e80100_resources },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,glymur-camss", .data = &glymur_resources },
 	{ }
 };
 
